  --raw-field body='Not applicable — TypeORM'\''s `QueryFailedError` constructor copies all `driverError` properties onto the error instance itself via `ObjectUtils.assign(this, { ...otherProperties })` ([source](https://github.com/typeorm/typeorm/blob/master/src/error/QueryFailedError.ts#L20-L25)). This means `error.code` **is** `'\''23505'\''` at runtime:

```js
const { QueryFailedError } = require("typeorm");
const pgErr = new Error("duplicate key");
pgErr.code = "23505";
const qfe = new QueryFailedError("INSERT ...", [], pgErr);
console.log(qfe.code); // "23505" ✓
```

Both `error.code` and `error.driverError.code` work; the current approach is correct.'

